
# Data Pipeline Starter 🇨🇲

A practical data engineering project focused on building a reliable procurement data pipeline using Python, data validation, cleaning, MySQL, analytics, machine learning, APIs, and cloud technologies.

The project uses a synthetic Cameroon public procurement dataset to simulate the challenges a data engineer may encounter when working with real-world procurement data.

> **Current status:** Phase 1 and Phase 2 completed.  
> Phase 3 will begin with data ingestion and validation.

# Project Overview

The long-term objective of this project is to build an end-to-end data pipeline following this architecture:

text
CSV / API
    ↓
Python
    ↓
Data Cleaning
    ↓
MySQL
    ↓
ETL Pipeline
    ↓
Analytics
    ↓
ML Model
    ↓
API / Dashboard

However, we are building the system incrementally.

At the current stage, we have completed:
text
Phase 1
Project Setup
     ↓
Phase 2
Synthetic Data Generation & Exploration

# Project Objectives

The project is designed to develop practical skills in:

* Data Engineering
* Python
* Data Cleaning
* Data Validation
* ETL
* MySQL
* Data Analytics
* Machine Learning
* REST APIs
* Cloud/DevOps
* Docker
* CI/CD

The emphasis is on understanding **why** each component is needed and how the components eventually work together as one data system.

# Current Technology Stack

At the current stage, we are primarily using:

| Technology       | Purpose                          |
| ---------------- | -------------------------------- |
| Python           | Core programming language        |
| Pandas           | Data exploration and analysis    |
| CSV              | Current data source              |
| Jupyter Notebook | Data exploration                 |
| Git              | Version control                  |
| GitHub           | Repository and collaboration     |
| Python `venv`    | Isolated development environment |

Future technologies such as MySQL, FastAPI, Docker, AWS, and machine learning frameworks will be introduced in later phases.

